        "description": "<p>Have our leaders ever done a cost-benefit analysis of Net Zero? If they had, they'd realise that Britain will pay \u00a3695bn just to make the world 0.00376\u00b0C less warm by 2100. How can that be worth it, asks Matt Ridley.</p>\n<p>The post <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://dailysceptic.org/2026/11/13/if-britain-reaches-its-net-zero-target-the-world-is-projected-to-be-0-00376c-less-warm-by-2100-is-that-really-worth-695-billion/\">If Britain Reaches its Net Zero Target, the World is Projected to Be 0.00376\u00b0C Less Warm by 2100. Is That Really Worth \u00a3695 Billion?</a> appeared first on <a rel=\"nofollow\" href=\"https://dailysceptic.org\">The Daily Sceptic</a>.</p>",
